---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const effective = '17 November 2026';
const contact = 'noah@stillpointlabs.dev';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — Stillpoint Labs"
  description="What Stillpoint Labs keeps for Reveal, Ingle and Troth, who else handles it, and how to delete it."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">We keep only what the work needs.</h1>
      <p class="effective fine">Effective {effective}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="policy">
    <div class="container-narrow prose">
      <p class="lede">
        Stillpoint Labs makes Reveal, Ingle and Troth, and all three share one Stillpoint
        account. We keep what you put into them so they can do their work for you. We do not
        sell your data, show you ads, or train AI models on it without your separate, explicit
        consent.
      </p>

      <h2>What this covers</h2>
      <p>
        This policy covers stillpointlabs.dev and the Stillpoint account you use to sign in to
        Reveal (app.reveal.photo), Ingle (app.ingle.kitchen) and Troth (app.troth.money). Each
        product's own site can add detail for that product. Questions go to
        <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your Stillpoint account</h2>
      <p>
        One account, keyed to one email address, works across all three apps. You sign in with
        a link we email you, or with Google where an app offers it. For the account we keep:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>your email address and an account ID</li>
        <li>a display name, taken from your Google profile or your email address</li>
        <li>sign-in records, including the time and IP address of each sign-in, for security</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Signing in with Google</h2>
      <p>
        When you choose Continue with Google, Google sends us your email address, whether Google
        has verified it, your name, your profile picture and a Google account ID. We ask Google
        for nothing else: no access to your Gmail, Drive, Calendar, Contacts or any other Google
        data. We use what Google sends for three things:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Email and account ID</strong> — to sign you in and match you to your existing
          Stillpoint account, so one email never becomes two accounts.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Name</strong> — as your display name inside the apps.</li>
        <li><strong>Profile picture</strong> — stored with your sign-in record; apps may show it next to your name.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Our sign-in provider, Supabase, stores this Google data, and it goes to no one else. We
        do not sell it, use it for advertising, or use it to develop, improve or train AI or
        machine-learning models. Nobody at Stillpoint Labs reads it unless you ask us to, it is
        needed for security, or the law requires it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stillpoint Labs' use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener"
          >Google API Services User Data Policy</a
        >, including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>
      <p>
        To remove our access, open your
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">Google Account permissions</a>
        and remove Stillpoint Labs. You can still sign in with an emailed link.
      </p>

      <h2>What each app keeps</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Reveal</strong> — the photographs you submit, with their embedded details
          (camera settings and, when present, GPS location); the developed images and artist
          statements made from them; your ratings and feedback.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ingle</strong> — your pantry, grocery lists, shopping trips and purchase
          history, including orders you import; budgets and meal plans; your household's members
          and their dietary preferences; photos you take to add pantry items.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Troth</strong> — your accounts (name, type, and only the last four digits of
          the number), transactions, balances, bills, income and goals. It comes from what you
          type, from CSV files you upload (we keep the rows and do not store the file), or from
          Plaid if you connect a bank.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Each app also keeps operational logs, which we use to fix problems and protect the service.</p>

      <h2>AI features</h2>
      <p>
        The apps use AI models from Anthropic (Claude) and Google (Gemini). We send each one only
        what the feature in front of you needs:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Reveal</strong> — your photograph and our notes on it to Anthropic, and the
          photograph with developing instructions to Google.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Ingle</strong> — pantry photos and item details to Anthropic, to identify what you have.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Troth</strong> — payee names to Anthropic for automatic categorization; when you
          use Ask, your question and the account data needed to answer it.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you connect Claude or another assistant to Ingle or Troth, it reads and changes your
        data through the access you approve, and its maker's terms cover what it does with that
        data. Disconnect it in the assistant's settings to end that access.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else handles your data</h2>
      <p>
        Besides the AI providers above, a few service providers run parts of the service, and
        each receives only what its part needs:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — database, file storage and sign-in, for all three apps.</li>
        <li><strong>Plaid</strong> — Troth's bank connections, only if you connect a bank.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting providers</strong> — run our websites, apps and photo processing.</li>
        <li><strong>Email services</strong> — deliver sign-in links and household invitations.</li>
        <li><strong>Mailing-list services</strong> — product waitlists and newsletters, only if you sign up.</li>
        <li><strong>A mapping service</strong> — a Reveal photo's GPS coordinates, to name the place.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell your data or share it for advertising. We disclose it beyond these
        providers only when the law requires it, or to a company that takes over Stillpoint
        Labs, which would then be bound by this policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site and the apps use cookies and browser storage only to keep you signed in and
        remember your settings. None of them run advertising or analytics trackers.
      </p>

      <h2>Keeping and deleting your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We keep your data while your account is open.</li>
        <li>
          To delete your account, email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a> from the
          address on the account. We delete the account and its data in all three apps within 30
          days. If you share a household, its shared records stay with the other members.
        </li>
        <li>Write to the same address for a copy of your data or to correct it.</li>
        <li>Every mailing-list email carries an unsubscribe link.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Data travels over HTTPS, and database rules limit each account to its own household's
        data. If a breach exposes your data, we will tell you.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Accounts are for adults. A parent can list children as members of an Ingle household,
        with their dietary preferences, and we treat that like the rest of the household's data.
        We do not knowingly open accounts for children under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        When this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it. If a change affects data
        you have already given us, we email you before it takes effect.
      </p>

      <p class="meta fine">
        Stillpoint Labs LLC, Utah · <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--space-16) 0 var(--space-8);
  }

  .page-hero .container-narrow {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .page-title {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
  }

  .policy {
    padding: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-12);
  }

  .policy .prose p,
  .policy .prose li {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--pitch-light);
  }

  .policy .prose .lede {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }

  .policy ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .policy li {
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .policy li::before {
    content: '—';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--mid);
  }

  .policy strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--pitch);
  }

  .meta {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }
</style>
